              "text": "جٹنا — juṭnā — \"to get down to (a task); to apply oneself\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اگر سب جٹ گئے تو کام جلدی ختم ہو گا۔ agar sab juṭ gae to kām jaldī khatm ho gā. If everyone gets down to work, it will soon be done."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): وہ کام میں جٹ گیا, voh kām meṅ juṭ gayā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جٹنا (juṭnā) is inherited: CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin juṭnā, \"to come together\", under yuṭati, a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 10496); the sense \"to throw oneself into a task\" is a later one our sources do not trace."
            }
          ]
        },
